## Part A: Demo Runner Toolbar

**Label Definitions:**

The toolbar labels are defined in [tools/demo/runner/main.ts](tools/demo/runner/main.ts#L191) at **line 191**:
```typescript
const labels: Record<PartKey, string> = { html: "HTML", css: "CSS", js: "JS" };
```

The "Result" tab label is added at [line 490](tools/demo/runner/main.ts#L490):
```typescript
addTab(ctx, "result", "Result");
```

**Toolbar Markup Construction:**

The static shell is built in `runnerMarkup()` function at [line 225](tools/demo/runner/main.ts#L225):
```typescript
return `<div class="runner runner--show-result runner--booting">
      <div class="runner__bar">
        <fieldset class="instui-radio-input-group -variant-toggle">
          <legend class="instui-screen-reader-content">View</legend>
        </fieldset>
      </div>
```

Dynamic tabs are created by `addTab()` at [lines 472–486](tools/demo/runner/main.ts#L472):
```typescript
function addTab(ctx: RunnerCtx, name: string, label: string): void {
  const wrapper = document.createElement("label");
  wrapper.className = "instui-radio -variant-toggle -size-sm";
  const input = document.createElement("input");
  input.type = "radio";
  input.name = "runner-view";
  input.value = name;
  input.addEventListener("change", () => {
    if (input.checked) select(ctx, name);
  });
  wrapper.append(input, document.createTextNode(` ${label}`));
  ctx.tablist.appendChild(wrapper);
}
```

**Locale Awareness:**

The runner itself does **not** have built-in localization for tab labels (they remain English). However:
- The broader demo system supports locale routing via `demoMarkdownIt` with a `localePrefix` option (see [tools/demo/src/index.ts](tools/demo/src/index.ts#L196))
- Locale-specific demo directories can be served by routing through `localePrefix` (tested in [tools/demo/tests/index.test.ts](tools/demo/tests/index.test.ts#L98))
- The runner page itself doesn't inherit `lang`/`dir` from its parent (it's an isolated iframe)

**RTL Direction:**

The runner detects RTL via `isRtl()` at [lines 57–61](tools/demo/runner/main.ts#L57):
```typescript
function isRtl(): boolean {
  try {
    if (window.parent && window.parent !== window) {
      return window.parent.document.documentElement.dir === "rtl";
    }
  } catch {
    // Cross-origin parent.
  }
  return false;
}
```

The result iframe receives `dir="rtl"` or `dir="ltr"` at [line 336](tools/demo/runner/main.ts#L336):
```typescript
ctx.resultFrame.srcdoc =
    `<!doctype html><html dir="${isRtl() ? "rtl" : "ltr"}" data-pantoken-theme="${ctx.currentTheme}" ...
```

**PostMessage Communication:**

The runner posts size and receives theme/scheme updates via postMessage:
- Size reports: [line 241](tools/demo/runner/main.ts#L241) and sizeReporter script at [line 334](tools/demo/runner/main.ts#L334)
- Theme request: [line 651](tools/demo/runner/main.ts#L651) `postMessage({ type: "pantoken-demo-request-theme" }, ...)`
- Result frame freeze message handling: sizeReporter script accepts `pantoken-demo-freeze` type

**Build & Serving:**

Build config in [tools/demo/vite.runner.config.ts](tools/demo/vite.runner.config.ts):
```typescript
// Emits to dist/runner/ with relative asset URLs (base "./")
export default defineConfig({
  root: fileURLToPath(new URL("./runner", import.meta.url)),
  base: "./",
  build: {
    outDir: fileURLToPath(new URL("./dist/runner", import.meta.url)),
  },
});
```

Build scripts in [tools/demo/vite.config.ts](tools/demo/vite.config.ts):
```typescript
run: { tasks: { build: { command: ["vp pack", "vp build -c vite.runner.config.ts"] } } }
```

The runner's default path is `play/index.html` (fallback in [tools/demo/src/index.ts](tools/demo/src/index.ts#L93)).

---

## Part B: Inline Code Styling & RTL

**Prose Rule Source:**

Located in [formats/components/src/rules/prose/index.ts](formats/components/src/rules/prose/index.ts).

**Code/Pre Styling** at [lines 94–102](formats/components/src/rules/prose/index.ts#L94):
```typescript
${s} code {
  font-family: var(--instui-font-family-code);
  font-size: 0.9em;
  background: var(--instui-color-background-muted);
  padding: var(--instui-spacing-space2xs) var(--instui-spacing-space-xs);
  border-radius: var(--instui-border-radius-sm);
}
${s} pre {
  font-family: var(--instui-font-family-code);
  background: var(--instui-color-background-container);
  color: var(--instui-color-text-base);
  padding: var(--instui-spacing-space-md);
  border: var(--instui-border-width-sm) solid var(--instui-color-stroke-base);
  border-radius: var(--instui-border-radius-md);
  overflow-x: auto;
}
${s} pre code { background: none; padding: 0; border-radius: 0; font-size: inherit; }
```

**RTL Handling in formats/components:**

Most components use **logical properties** (`flex-direction`, `inset-inline-*`) that automatically respect `direction` and `dir="rtl"`:
- Breadcrumb: [formats/components/src/components/breadcrumb/members/link/link.css](formats/components/src/components/breadcrumb/members/link/link.css#L7) includes explicit `[dir="rtl"]` selector for chevron mirroring
- Tray: [formats/components/src/components/tray/tray.css](formats/components/src/components/tray/tray.css#L16) uses `inset-inline` (RTL-safe) with automatic transform mirroring under `[dir="rtl"]`
- Drawer-layout: [formats/components/src/components/drawer-layout/drawer-layout.css](formats/components/src/components/drawer-layout/drawer-layout.css#L15) remarks: "flex-direction/inset-inline-* logical properties, not left/right, so the tray's side follows direction/dir="rtl" automatically"

**Direction Propagation to Demo Documents:**

1. **In `/play` runner** ([tools/demo/runner/main.ts](tools/demo/runner/main.ts#L336)):
   ```typescript
   ctx.resultFrame.srcdoc = `<!doctype html><html dir="${isRtl() ? "rtl" : "ltr"}" ...`
   ```

2. **In `srcdoc` iframe** ([tools/demo/src/srcdoc.ts](tools/demo/src/srcdoc.ts#L67)):
   ```typescript
   `<!doctype html><html dir="${options.dir ?? "ltr"}"><head>...`
   ```
   The `dir` option is part of `ExampleSrcdocOptions` (default `"ltr"`, [line 21](tools/demo/src/srcdoc.ts#L21)), passed by markdown-it plugin from the page's locale context.

